          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: Witnesses observed at 23:00 the silent passage of a dozen red objects in the sky. The observation of red or orange balls flying in the sky for several minutes, on a Saturday evening, clearly evokes Thai lanterns released after a party. The weather report for Lyon Bron (attached) indicates a very low and unstable wind: it is not possible to estimate the wind direction at that time and correlate it with the observation. However, it is noted that the objects flew slowly, which is consistent with a weak wind. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
